  "usage_note": "**A lot of** and **lots of** are common in all kinds of sentences in everyday English. In formal writing, **much**, **many**, or **a great deal of** is often better. **A lot** used without a noun to mean *very much* or *often* (*I like it a lot*; *We go there a lot*) is an adverb; see that entry.",
  "learner_errors": [
    {
      "incorrect": "There are a lot people here.",
      "correct": "There are a lot of people here.",
      "note": "Put **of** after **a lot** before a noun."
    },
    {
      "incorrect": "I have alot of friends.",
      "correct": "I have a lot of friends.",
      "note": "**A lot** is always two words."
    }
